<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41144" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕpărābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		reparo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be repaired</i>, <i>restored</i>, or <i>regained; retrievable</i>, <i>reparable</i> (mostly <b>poet.</b>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not anteAug.): damnum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 379</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 1, 14, 55</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laesa pudicitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					5, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 562</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Vit. Beat. 6, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 3</span></i>: ales phoenix, i. e. <i>coming</i>
			
			
			<i>to life again</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus.
				Idyll. 18, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">echo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>repeating</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 102</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Always ready</i>, <i>alert</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reparabilis gentis motus infidi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 10, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barbarique ut reparabiles semper et celeres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 31, 7, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
